  "articleBody": "When it comes to ramp repair, it's easy to make a few common blunders that can turn a small issue into a bigger headache. First off, a frequent mistake is treating surface wear as purely cosmetic. You might think a little scuff or faded paint is no big deal, but it could be a sign of deeper issues, especially if the surface is losing its slip resistance. Another common oversight? Ignoring loose fasteners. A wobbly ramp might just need some tightening, but delaying that simple fix can lead to structural damage over time. It's like ignoring a small crack in your windshield – it usually just gets worse! Also, delaying repairs after you spot visible damage or notice a wobble is a huge no-no. Small issues often become bigger, more expensive problems, and more importantly, they become safety risks. Periodic checks are your best friend here, helping you catch things before they escalate. If you’re ever unsure about whether something is cosmetic or structural, or if you just don’t have the right tools or expertise, that’s where HH Remodeling LLC can step in. We're happy to assess the damage and make sure your ramp is safe and sound for folks in Denver, Centennial, and all the surrounding communities.",
